FerrionOS change to upstream userutils (MIT license, kept), made against upstream commit 641a5aa81574db79d883151bc3438d3e59f90b88 after the existing recipe patches.

One password: login and the new unlock-session command (for the graphical login) start the first session of the account whose key slot opened the volume at startup without a password, once per boot, reading the slot from /scheme/sys/env and the account from the root-only /etc/unlock-slots, never after a recovery-key unlock. The once-per-boot claim is tracked through UnlockState and stored inside /var/run/unlock-session (root-owned, mode 0700, created and cleared at boot by 00_unlock_claim), refusing symlinks and failing closed when the directory is missing or has group or other permissions. passwd changes that account's disk slot through redoxfs-key change in the sudo daemon, in the same operation, asking for the previous disk password (or recovery key) when the current login password cannot open the slot after an administrator reset, and fails without changing the shadow file when the slot cannot be changed; a password set by root without the old one says the disk keeps the old one. Root can enroll an account with a non-empty password through passwd --enroll LOGIN, and userdel revokes an enrolled account's disk slot before removing the account.

